{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The New Waiter", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Getting Comfortable", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about people's interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " A phrasal verb is made from a verb and one more particles. Particles and prepositions look the same but they have different jobs. Prepositions DO NOT change the meaning of the main verb. Particles usually change the meaning of the main verb.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Phrasal verbs can be separable or inseparable. <br> With a separable phrasal verb, the object can go after the particle or between the verb and the particle. <br> Example: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">I picked out a dress.</span>    or <span class=\"italic\">  I picked a dress out.</span><br> NOTE: If the object is a pronoun, it must go between the particle and the verb. <br> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">I picked it out.</span> NOT <span class=\"italic\"> I picked out it.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " The verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <ul><li>call off = cancel<br/>    <span class=\"italic\">They called off the meeting.</span></li> <li>pick out = choose <br/>   I picked out a new dress.</span></li> <li>take away = remove   <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Please take away that garbage.</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the following inseparable phrasal verbs to describe life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to hang around\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to spend time with someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to look down on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to feel superior to someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to look up to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to admire someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to talk back\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to answer impolitely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to put up with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to tolerate\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I really looked up to my mentor. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For example, he gave me pointers on how to put up with difficult customers in any situation.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Should and Be Supposed To ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modal  <span class=\"strong\">should</span> or the  structure  <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use  <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the present or future that are expected to happen. <br/><br/> The structure is:<br/><br/>  Subject + To be + supposed to + verb<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Sharing information with their new colleagues is something they're <span class=\"strong\">supposed to do</span> .</span> <br/><br/>  **Pronunciation tip**:<br/> When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together.  <br/><br/> Like this:<br/> Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You're supposed to keep smiling even when you have to deal with terrible patrons. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Obviously, you shouldn't talk back either.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "trainee", "type": "name"}, {"content": " someone undergoing training", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a new trainee, you should spend some time with a senior waiter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you talk about customer service.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hang around", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time with someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a new trainee, you should hang around with a senior waiter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to look down on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel superior to someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope the senior waiters won't look down on me because I'm a trainee.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to look up to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "respect, admire someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I had a mentor in Colombia that I really looked up to you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to talk back", "type": "name"}, {"content": "respond in an impolite way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Servers should not talk back to customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to put up with", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to tolerate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to put up with difficult customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "impeccable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without any faults", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  His service is impeccable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unobtrusive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unnoticeable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is an unobtrusive server. Patrons barely notice him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a paragraph 6 to 8 sentences long.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Who was your most important mentor when you were young?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Why did you pick this person?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What problems did your mentor help you with?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What rules and regulations did they teach you?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use at least five phrasal verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your story with your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about a mentor.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain why I picked the person. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use phrasal verbs", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [